    <briefdescription>
<para>A name of a suite or of a test case, with the location where it was given. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The name parameter of <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1suite_1a0cfa76ba0ba0c308d246b2b5d506ab19" kindref="member">suite::test()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case_1a9b497f0911a0abe12a341a560ba79e1d" kindref="member">test_case::test()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput>test_each()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1abdb31c03509a40a041b8f0ea8e12ebd1" kindref="member">runner::add_suite()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1a9ec7d561fe8eab9df03da792f62518ae" kindref="member">runner::add_top_suite()</ref></computeroutput>, and the <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1static__suite" kindref="compound">static_suite</ref></computeroutput> constructors. The constructors are not explicit, so a string literal, a <computeroutput>const char*</computeroutput>, a <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput>, or a <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> passed as the name converts implicitly; the default argument of the constructors is evaluated at the place of the conversion, which is the call in the user code, so the location is captured without an additional argument (which could not follow the variadic arguments of these functions).</para>
<para>The name is copied, so the argument need not outlive the call, and a <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> need not be null-terminated; a temporary <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> is moved. The copy of a test case name lives until the end of the call to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, within which the test case runs, so the memory used does not grow with the number of test cases; the suites, which run later, keep their name, moved, until they are destroyed.</para>
<para>The location of a test case is used to report a failure that is not associated with a check, such as an exception escaping the test case body; the suites keep their location, but do not report it.</para>
<para>Since a conversion sequence may include only one user-defined conversion, an argument that converts to <computeroutput>const char*</computeroutput>, to <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput>, or to <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> via a user-defined conversion operator must be converted explicitly.</para>
<para>A helper function that adds test cases on behalf of its caller can take a <computeroutput>const <ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1located__name" kindref="compound">located_name</ref>&amp;</computeroutput> parameter and pass it to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, so that the reported location is that of the call to the helper, not that of the call to <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput> inside the helper.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">check_answer<sp/>(mt::suite&amp;<sp/>ts,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>mt::located_name&amp;<sp/><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1located__name_1aa2ec3a20974c59b2f5a64a50b41db444" kindref="member">name</ref>,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>v)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>ts.test<sp/>(<ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1located__name_1aa2ec3a20974c59b2f5a64a50b41db444" kindref="member">name</ref>,<sp/>[v]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{<sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(v,<sp/>42));<sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
